  "description": "K-way external merge sort for .NET 8. Sort datasets larger than available memory using binary min-heap merge. v1.0.5 copies the already-sorted final chunk to the output verbatim instead of re-serializing it (one fewer deserialization pass — ~8% less allocation, faster). Builds on the v1.0.4 parallel merge (~1.54x end-to-end vs the old serial-merge ~1.20x ceiling) plus option validation, leak-safe streams, Int64 counts for billion-record sorts, real BytesRead/BytesWritten metrics, pipelined parallel chunk creation, Knuth's Replacement Selection, and a ReplaceMin merge fast path. Generic IExternalSorter<T> — plug in any record type, comparer, and serializer.",
